[0.45, "o", "Title:      \u001b[1mExport Canonical Hosted Cluster Truth And Seal Managed Lifecycle Ownership\u001b[0m\r\nStatus:     \u001b[32machieved\u001b[39m\r\nArchetype:  \u001b[95m\u001b[1mStrategic\u001b[0m\u001b[39m\r\n\u001b[2m\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[1mGoals\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mMG-01\u001b[0m - Deliver epic `VGcgU7q58` so Port exposes one canonical hosted-cluster status contract with machine, placement, managed-service, and legacy-runtime truth that downstream `infra` can consume directly. (\u001b[2mVGcgU7q58\u001b[0m)\r\n  \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mMG-02\u001b[0m - Deliver epic `VGcgU9T57` so hosted K3s lifecycle stays under explicit Port-managed service ownership, including placement persistence, legacy-path rejection, and durability proof. (\u001b[2mVGcgU9T57\u001b[0m)\r\n\r\n\u001b[1mChildren\u001b[0m\r\n  Epics (2):\r\n    \u001b[1m\u001b[36mVGcgU9T57\u001b[39m\u001b[0m - Seal Managed Hosted Service Ownership (\u001b[2mdone\u001b[0m)\r\n    \u001b[1m\u001b[36mVGcgU7q58\u001b[39m\u001b[0m - Export Canonical Hosted Cluster Status Contract (\u001b[2mdone\u001b[0m)\r\n\r\n\u001b[1mStructural Drift\u001b[0m\r\n  Coefficient: 0.63 (severe)\r\n  Coverage:    entities 302/302 | knowledge 5/45 | source 0/0 | docs 0/17\r\n  Context:     40 knowledge units lack source provenance; 17 project docs are unlinked\r\n\r\n\u001b[1mLatest Log Entry\u001b[0m\r\n    2026-04-12T16:55:04\r\n"]
[1.8, "o", "$ sed -n '1,120p' .keel/missions/VGcgTAwn4/CHARTER.md\r\n"]
[2.25, "o", "# Export Canonical Hosted Cluster Truth And Seal Managed Lifecycle Ownership - Charter\r\n\r\nArchetype: Strategic\r\n\r\n## Goals\r\n\r\n| ID | Description | Verification |\r\n|----|-------------|--------------|\r\n| MG-01 | Deliver epic `VGcgU7q58` so Port exposes one canonical hosted-cluster status contract with machine, placement, managed-service, and legacy-runtime truth that downstream `infra` can consume directly. | board: VGcgU7q58 |\r\n| MG-02 | Deliver epic `VGcgU9T57` so hosted K3s lifecycle stays under explicit Port-managed service ownership, including placement persistence, legacy-path rejection, and durability proof. | board: VGcgU9T57 |\r\n\r\n## Constraints\r\n\r\n- Preserve the downstream contract on `port cluster up`, `port cluster status`,\r\n  and `port cluster kubeconfig`; the simplification belongs inside Port rather\r\n  than in downstream orchestration glue.\r\n- Keep hosted lifecycle ownership inside Port: placements, managed-service\r\n  truth, restart posture, and runtime drift detection should not require\r\n  `infra` reconstruction.\r\n- Treat legacy detached K3s PID/log artifacts as invalid runtime drift rather\r\n  than an alternate happy path for hosted clusters.\r\n- Make the status contract machine-readable and explicit enough for the paired\r\n  `infra` mission `VGcfT59ur` to consume without ad hoc probing.\r\n- Keep proof human-reviewable, with a specific focus on the 60-90 minute worker\r\n  stability failure mode seen in prod.\r\n\r\n## Halting Rules\r\n\r\n- DO NOT halt while any MG-* goal has unfinished board work\r\n- HALT when epics `VGcgU7q58` and `VGcgU9T57` are complete and the mission can\r\n  be achieved.\r\n- YIELD to human when the remaining blocker is a cross-repo schema or product\r\n  decision about hosted status semantics, proof expectations, or lifecycle\r\n  boundaries that cannot be resolved from repository context.\r\n"]
[3.6, "o", "$ keel epic show VGcgU7q58\r\n"]
[4.05, "o", "Title:     \u001b[1mExport Canonical Hosted Cluster Status Contract\u001b[0m\r\nStatus:    \u001b[32mdone\u001b[39m\r\nCreated:   \u001b[2m2026-04-12 16:37:34\u001b[0m\r\nStarted:   \u001b[2m2026-04-12 16:50:24\u001b[0m\r\nUpdated:   \u001b[2m2026-04-12 17:15:21\u001b[0m\r\nCompleted: \u001b[2m2026-04-12 17:15:21\u001b[0m (\u001b[2m24m\u001b[0m)\r\nPath:      \u001b[2m/home/alex/workspace/spoke-sh/port/.keel/epics/VGcgU7q58/README.md\u001b[0m\r\nPRD:       \u001b[2m/home/alex/workspace/spoke-sh/port/.keel/epics/VGcgU7q58/PRD.md\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2m\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[1mProblem\u001b[0m\r\n  Downstream infra still has to infer hosted cluster truth from placements, node readiness, and ad hoc service checks because Port does not yet expose one canonical hosted status contract with machine, service, and legacy-runtime truth.\r\n\r\n\u001b[1mGoals\u001b[0m\r\n  - \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mGOAL-01\u001b[0m: Expose one canonical hosted-cluster status contract that downstream consumers can trust for machines, placements, managed services, and legacy-runtime drift. (Downstream \u001b[38;2;230;237;243;48;2;48;54;61minfra\u001b[0m no longer needs to reconstruct hosted cluster truth from ad hoc probes. -> First canonical hosted status cutover)\r\n  - \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mGOAL-02\u001b[0m: Make hosted status explicit enough to drive downstream rollout, inspection, and reuse decisions safely. (The same Port status payload can power lifecycle and operator consumption without bespoke side channels. -> First downstream-ready contract)\r\n\r\n\u001b[1mScope Drift\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[2m(no scope drift detected)\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n\u001b[1mStructural Drift\u001b[0m\r\n  Coefficient: 0.63 (severe)\r\n  Coverage:    entities 302/302 | knowledge 5/45 | source 0/0 | docs 0/17\r\n  Context:     40 knowledge units lack source provenance; 17 project docs are unlinked\r\n\r\n\u001b[1mRequirement Coverage\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[36mFR-01\u001b[39m - Port must expose one canonical hosted-cluster status contract that includes machine identity, placement, managed-service state, and legacy detached-runtime drift.\r\n    Linked goals (1): \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mGOAL-01\u001b[0m\r\n    Linked children (1): \u001b[1m\u001b[35mVGcghuutu\u001b[39m\u001b[0m/\u001b[36mSRS-01\u001b[39m\r\n  \u001b[36mFR-02\u001b[39m - The canonical hosted status contract must be available through existing cluster status surfaces rather than a one-off diagnostic path.\r\n    Linked goals (2): \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mGOAL-01\u001b[0m, \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mGOAL-02\u001b[0m\r\n    Linked children (1): \u001b[1m\u001b[35mVGcghuutu\u001b[39m\u001b[0m/\u001b[36mSRS-02\u001b[39m\r\n  \u001b[36mFR-03\u001b[39m - The hosted status contract must remain explicit enough for downstream consumers to distinguish healthy managed services from legacy detached K3s artifacts. (uncovered)\r\n    Linked goals (1): \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mGOAL-02\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[36mFR-04\u001b[39m - Port must document the downstream contract and proof expectations for the hosted status payload.\r\n    Linked goals (1): \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mGOAL-02\u001b[0m\r\n    Linked children (1): \u001b[1m\u001b[35mVGcghuutu\u001b[39m\u001b[0m/\u001b[36mSRS-03\u001b[39m\r\n  \u001b[36mNFR-01\u001b[39m - The hosted status contract must stay machine-readable and stable enough to be consumed without downstream schema forks.\r\n    Linked goals (2): \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mGOAL-01\u001b[0m, \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mGOAL-02\u001b[0m\r\n    Linked children (1): \u001b[1m\u001b[35mVGcghuutu\u001b[39m\u001b[0m/\u001b[36mSRS-NFR-01\u001b[39m\r\n  \u001b[36mNFR-02\u001b[39m - The new surface must not introduce a second contradictory truth source for hosted lifecycle state.\r\n    Linked goals (1): \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mGOAL-01\u001b[0m\r\n    Linked children (1): \u001b[1m\u001b[35mVGcghuutu\u001b[39m\u001b[0m/\u001b[36mSRS-NFR-02\u001b[39m\r\n\r\n\u001b[1mPress Release\u001b[0m\r\n  Status:     \u001b[2mnot authored\u001b[0m\r\n  Guidance:   optional; use for large user-facing value shifts\r\n\r\n\u001b[1mProgress\u001b[0m\r\n  Voyages:              1/1 \u001b[32m\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u001b[39m \u001b[32m1/1\u001b[39m\r\n  Stories:              3/3 \u001b[32m\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u001b[39m \u001b[32m3/3\u001b[39m\r\n  ETA:                  complete\r\n\r\n\u001b[1mVerification Strategy\u001b[0m\r\n  Techniques:\r\n    - Area: Method\r\n    - Contract documentation: Authored doc review\r\n    - Downstream readiness: Cross-repo manual proof\r\n    - Status schema: Targeted automated coverage plus CLI proof\r\n\r\n\u001b[1mVerification Readiness\u001b[0m\r\n  Criteria:              automated 5 | manual 2\r\n  Requirement coverage:  automated 4 | manual 1\r\n  Artifact inventory:    text 7 | media 0 | other 0\r\n\r\n\u001b[1mVoyages\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[1m\u001b[35mVGcghuutu\u001b[39m\u001b[0m - Expose Hosted Cluster Status Schema (\u001b[32mdone\u001b[39m)\r\n"]
[5.4, "o", "$ keel epic show VGcgU9T57\r\n"]
[5.85, "o", "Title:     \u001b[1mSeal Managed Hosted Service Ownership\u001b[0m\r\nStatus:    \u001b[32mdone\u001b[39m\r\nCreated:   \u001b[2m2026-04-12 16:37:34\u001b[0m\r\nStarted:   \u001b[2m2026-04-12 17:15:58\u001b[0m\r\nUpdated:   \u001b[2m2026-04-12 17:45:19\u001b[0m\r\nCompleted: \u001b[2m2026-04-12 17:45:19\u001b[0m (\u001b[2m29m\u001b[0m)\r\nPath:      \u001b[2m/home/alex/workspace/spoke-sh/port/.keel/epics/VGcgU9T57/README.md\u001b[0m\r\nPRD:       \u001b[2m/home/alex/workspace/spoke-sh/port/.keel/epics/VGcgU9T57/PRD.md\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2m\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[1mProblem\u001b[0m\r\n  Hosted K3s machines can still drift into stale placement or legacy detached service paths, which leaves worker recovery and downstream inspection dependent on implicit runtime behavior instead of managed Port service ownership.\r\n\r\n\u001b[1mGoals\u001b[0m\r\n  - \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mGOAL-01\u001b[0m: Keep hosted K3s lifecycle under explicit Port-managed service ownership across launch, reuse, and recovery. (Workers and servers remain represented as managed services instead of legacy detached processes. -> First fully owned hosted lifecycle slice)\r\n  - \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mGOAL-02\u001b[0m: Make hosted worker stability provable over the observed 60-90 minute failure window. (Soak-oriented proof exists for managed hosted workers and their recovery posture. -> First durability proof slice)\r\n\r\n\u001b[1mScope Drift\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[2m(no scope drift detected)\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n\u001b[1mStructural Drift\u001b[0m\r\n  Coefficient: 0.63 (severe)\r\n  Coverage:    entities 302/302 | knowledge 5/45 | source 0/0 | docs 0/17\r\n  Context:     40 knowledge units lack source provenance; 17 project docs are unlinked\r\n\r\n\u001b[1mRequirement Coverage\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[36mFR-01\u001b[39m - Port must persist hosted placement and managed-service records durably enough that reuse, service status, and recovery do not depend on transient launch-time state.\r\n    Linked goals (1): \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mGOAL-01\u001b[0m\r\n    Linked children (1): \u001b[1m\u001b[35mVGcghwZrb\u001b[39m\u001b[0m/\u001b[36mSRS-01\u001b[39m\r\n  \u001b[36mFR-02\u001b[39m - Port must reject, replace, or otherwise eliminate legacy detached hosted K3s paths in favor of managed-service ownership.\r\n    Linked goals (1): \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mGOAL-01\u001b[0m\r\n    Linked children (1): \u001b[1m\u001b[35mVGcghwZrb\u001b[39m\u001b[0m/\u001b[36mSRS-02\u001b[39m\r\n  \u001b[36mFR-03\u001b[39m - Port must provide proof that hosted worker lifecycle remains healthy over the observed 60-90 minute drift window or recovers correctly when it does not.\r\n    Linked goals (1): \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mGOAL-02\u001b[0m\r\n    Linked children (1): \u001b[1m\u001b[35mVGcghwZrb\u001b[39m\u001b[0m/\u001b[36mSRS-03\u001b[39m\r\n  \u001b[36mNFR-01\u001b[39m - The managed-service ownership model must remain explicit in runtime artifacts and service-status surfaces rather than hidden in shell behavior.\r\n    Linked goals (1): \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mGOAL-01\u001b[0m\r\n    Linked children (1): \u001b[1m\u001b[35mVGcghwZrb\u001b[39m\u001b[0m/\u001b[36mSRS-NFR-01\u001b[39m\r\n  \u001b[36mNFR-02\u001b[39m - Durability proof must be reviewable without private workstation lore.\r\n    Linked goals (1): \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mGOAL-02\u001b[0m\r\n    Linked children (1): \u001b[1m\u001b[35mVGcghwZrb\u001b[39m\u001b[0m/\u001b[36mSRS-NFR-02\u001b[39m\r\n\r\n\u001b[1mPress Release\u001b[0m\r\n  Status:     \u001b[2mnot authored\u001b[0m\r\n  Guidance:   optional; use for large user-facing value shifts\r\n\r\n\u001b[1mProgress\u001b[0m\r\n  Voyages:              1/1 \u001b[32m\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u001b[39m \u001b[32m1/1\u001b[39m\r\n  Stories:              3/3 \u001b[32m\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u001b[39m \u001b[32m3/3\u001b[39m\r\n  ETA:                  complete\r\n\r\n\u001b[1mVerification Strategy\u001b[0m\r\n  Techniques:\r\n    - Area: Method\r\n    - Legacy-path elimination: CLI proof and regression inspection\r\n    - Placement/service durability: Automated coverage plus CLI proof\r\n    - Soak stability: Long-running proof\r\n\r\n\u001b[1mVerification Readiness\u001b[0m\r\n  Criteria:              automated 2 | manual 4\r\n  Requirement coverage:  automated 2 | manual 4\r\n  Artifact inventory:    text 6 | media 2 | other 2\r\n\r\n\u001b[1mVoyages\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[1m\u001b[35mVGcghwZrb\u001b[39m\u001b[0m - Seal Managed Hosted K3s Ownership (\u001b[32mdone\u001b[39m)\r\n"]
